There's also a version in C.

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Cadd9) and (Gadd) and add the 9th/5th note as necessary.
 
TIP:  You can play this song without the (Gadd) but it helps accentuate Emmylou's aching high notes. 

TIP:  You can play (D) and (G) in place of the (Cadd9) and (Gadd) combination in the first two  verses but it's easy to play as all you do from the leading (C) is "add" your pinky to the 2nd string/3rd fret.  Then rotate your wrist to play the upcoming (Gadd).  Plus it sounds prettier.  


